<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids mostly lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids mostly lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spring wheat cash bids remained mostly weaker on Monday amid lackluster activity, dealers said.</p>
<p>Merchandisers in Minnesota, North Dakota and Montana cited limited farm sales and a lack of export interest.</p>
<p>&quot;We had a truck here and a truck there,&quot; a Montana dealer said.</p>
<p>But another Montana merchandiser said spring plantings appeared to be on schedule in some areas and farmers were planning to start fieldwork in a week or so.</p>
<p>&quot;If the weather stays the way it is, fieldwork should be starting next week,&quot; the merchandiser said. &quot;Farmers were targeting $4.30 a bushel for spring wheat.&quot;</p>
